<Placemark>   <name>Barochan Cross</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Renfrewshire <b>Alt Name:</b> Kilpeter Celtic Cross / St. Fillan Cross <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.844911665075 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -4.420424750585<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/thumb/Barochan_Cross_2.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Renfrewshire. One of three remaining, complete Celtic Crosses that survive from the ancient Kingdom of Strathclyde, the other 2 being the 'Sun Cross' in Govan, and the 'Netherton Cros...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=51515" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-4.4204247505856,55.844911665075,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Boar Stone (Drem)</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> East Lothian <b>Alt Name:</b> New Mains; Boar Stone (Prora) <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.008310749498 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -2.764622433584<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Lothian/thumb/27thSeptember2017TheBoarStoneDremDSC_1055.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in East Lothian. This now broken cross shaft has been relocated to the garden of Prora Farm, some 1.35km east of Drem station at some time in the past.  Its original location is said to ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=47536" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-2.7646224335843,56.008310749498,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Camus Cross (Angus)</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Angus <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>2</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.530646558228 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -2.783570436773<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Angus/thumb/P1010005.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Early Cross in Angus. According to Elizabeth Sutherland in "The Pictish Guide" this is unusual in showing the crucifixion on one side. The Cross is on a small mound in the middle of a tree lined 'back...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=7715" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-2.7835704367735,56.530646558228,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Canongate Mercat Cross</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Midlothian <b>Alt Name:</b> Burgh Cross (Canongate); Canongate Kirk Cross <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.9516887985 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -3.179045692617<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Lothian/thumb/1stOct2019CanongateIMG_2994.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Midlothian. This cross has a plaque affixed to its front, proudly announcing it is the "Canongate Mercat Cross, 1128". It is sited at the eastern side of Canongate Kirk, on Canongate,...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=52438" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-3.1790456926173,55.9516887985,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Castleton (Newcastleton)</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Scottish Borders <b>Alt Name:</b> Old Castleton <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.200297630564 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -2.769797447150<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Borders/thumb/24thJune2017CastletonCrossLookingBackToB6357DS.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Scottish Borders. This badly damaged cross sits in rough pastures towards the edge of a field at Old Castleton, just over 150 metres from the south east edge of the Liddel Castle/Old ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=46936" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-2.7697974471507,55.200297630564,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Cavers Cross</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Scottish Borders <b>Alt Name:</b> Cavers Auld Kirk <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.432485153781 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -2.727375270469<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Borders/thumb/29thAugust2018CaversCrossDSC_2369.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Scottish Borders. The remains of this early medieval cross can be found near the Auld Kirk in the hamlet of Cavers, near Hawick.  Recorded as Canmore ID 55297.  Their latest entry was...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=50409" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-2.727375270469,55.432485153781,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Cockburnspath Cross</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Scottish Borders <b>Alt Name:</b> Cockburnspath Mercat Cross <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.932429589745 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -2.362821267075<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/scotland/Borders/thumb/29thSept2018CockburnspathLookingSWDSC_4080.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
